From the move to Kleve to the Opschlag, the sympathetic café lovers hope for more audiences.
Last but not least by the university.
"While we don't have a specific target group," emphasizes Daniel Büttner.
Rather, the two would like to appeal to young students as well as seniors and all age groups in between.
Speaking of cafe lovers.
The sympathetic pair of owners stands behind the coffee enjoyment.
Enjoy the fragrant hot brew in a variety of variations itself.
expressofan
Daniel Büttner is rather the Expresso fan and Mirjam van der Stelt the cappuccino drinker.
"A baguette - that's my thing," she reveals the NRZ.
There were also two events in the bright café.
Or rather, one thing.
Because the harbour festival took place rather outside - the Café Déjà Vu did not benefit from it.
But there was also the Ringelnatz evening.
"Beautiful, successful and witty," the two 33-year-old found.
But not everyone's cause.
Maybe that's why Daniel Büttner isn't an outspoken fan of event evenings either: "You can't please everyone".
And with an event, I always address only those who are also interested in the special event.
That’s why events will be the exception with us.
"We would like to disturb the normal operation as little as possible."
Déjà Vu also stands for reliability.
With regard to the quality of the products offered here, as well as to the team and the beautiful surroundings at Opschlag in Kleve.
The road that is developing more and more into a gastronomy mile.
To the delight of many Klever, the guests from near and far and the students who discover the gastrom reile and thus the Café Déjà Vu for themselves.
