Until May 23, Aufsteiger Düsseldorf Baskets can still submit documents to the arbitration court and prove his economic Bundesliga suitability.
So far, however, the Rhinelanders have been denied the license twice.
The arbitration tribunal is the last instance.
Haigerloch: Church of the Lord's Supper comes into focus
As a contribution of the city to the 150th anniversary of the Evangelical Church in Haigerloch, the City's Cultural and Tourism Office is dedicating the last of this year's public themed tours on Sunday, October 27 to the Lord's Supper Church.
After the visit to the Atomkeller Museum, the Haigerlocher period after 1850 is to be considered when Haigerloch came under Prussian rule.
The crunching conclusion is a visit to the Lord’s Supper Church.
There, the leaders are told the story of the construction of the church and gain insights into the development of the evangelical community in a thoroughly Catholic area.
Last but not least, in the church there is also a view of the Lord’s Supper painting created by Friedrich Schüz with the support of Walter Kröll and Georg Halbritter.
