Frankfurt parking fees to rise sharply
Parking in Frankfurt could soon become sensitively more expensive.
The city's magistrate is discussinging this morning on a submission by Transport Secretary Stefan Majer (Greens).
The parking fees are to be increased by 50 percent.
For this purpose, however, the prices should not be increased, but the time interval of parking meters and parking ticket machines should be shortened from 30 to 20 minutes.
In December, the city council has yet to decide.
The retail committee of the IHK Frankfurt considers this "not a good idea".
The possibility of parking directly in front of the shop is "a not to be underestimated advantage for smaller specialist retailers".
The Verkehrsclub Deutschland is of the opinion that an increase after two decades is "quite appropriate and actually long overdue".
Public transport will also be more expensive.
