Johannes Kana had already been found guilty earlier this week.
The act had sparked nationwide horror.
The 21-year-old had raped Anene Booysen in an industrial site in Bredasdorp near Cape Town in February.
Doctors spent 14 hours fighting for the victim’s survival, but in vain.
The sight of the young people was so horrifying that the nurses and nurses needed psychological assistance.
Kana had admitted during the trial to having been in a bar on the night of the crime with Booysen.
He also confessed to beating and raping her, but he denied being responsible for the girl's death.
The police had initially proceeded from several perpetrators, but dismissed two suspects from detention because the evidence against them was insufficient.
Prosecutors also stressed during the proceedings that she was convinced Kana was alone at the time of the attack.
